# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-Header SSO Bridge:**"
msgstr "**Trusted-Header SSO Bridge:**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-Header SSO Bridge:**   When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT's native `loginViaRemoteUser()` is enabled via the `Setting` model (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`). nginx gates `/login` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` header, which Snipe-IT matches against `users.username` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native `snipeit_session`. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (`login_common_disabled = 0`), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "**Trusted-Header SSO Bridge:** När oauth2Proxy SSO smak är aktiv, Snipe-ITs infödda `loginViaRemoteUser()` aktiveras via `Setting` modell (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`). nginx portar `/login` genom oauth2Proxy/Keycloak och injicerar den verifierade `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` header, som Snipe-IT matchar mot `users.username` (Användaren måste existera och aktiveras – synkronisera dem via LDAP) Att mynta en infödd `snipeit_session`. Besökare utan en matchande aktiverad användare faller tyst igenom till det normala inloggningsformuläret (Inget fel)Lösenordet / LDAP inloggningsformuläret förblir tillgängligt som en nedgång (`login_common_disabled = 0`), och in-app inloggningen omdirigeras till den centrala OIDC end-session URL."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-header SSO bridge:** Establishes the owner session from the oauth2-proxy identity (see below)."
msgstr "**Trusted-header SSO bridge:** Etablerar ägarsessionen från oauth2proxy identitet (Se nedan)."

