# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Clients do not read the server list directly. [`lookup('mcp_servers')`](../../../../../plugins/lookup/mcp_servers.py) computes the intersection of the provider's admitted clients, resolved by `derive_allowed_consumers` in [`utils/roles/applications/mcp.py`](../../../../../utils/roles/applications/mcp.py), with the calling client's `supported_transports` and `supported_auths`, resolves each provider's declared credential, and returns:"
msgstr "Kunderna läser inte serverlistan direkt. [`lookup('mcp_servers')`](../../../../../plugins/lookup/mcp_servers.py) beräknar korsningen av leverantörens antagna kunder, löst av `derive_allowed_consumers` in i [`utils/roles/applications/mcp.py`](../../../../../utils/roles/applications/mcp.py), med den ringande klientens `supported_transports` och `supported_auths`, löser varje leverantörs deklarerade referenser och returnerar:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Clients present a Gitea personal access token as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. The token is issued against the administrator account and kept in `sys-token-store`. Its `auth_subject` is `administrator`, so MCP calls run with administrator rights rather than as the requesting user."
msgstr "Kunder presenterar en Gitea Personlig tillgång token som `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Token utfärdas mot administratörskontot och hålls i `sys-token-store`. Dess `auth_subject` är att `administrator`, MCP-samtal körs med administratörsrättigheter snarare än som den begärande användaren."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Clients present a Gitea personal access token as ``Authorization: Bearer <token>``. The token is issued against the administrator account and kept in ``sys-token-store``. Its ``auth_subject`` is ``administrator``, so MCP calls run with administrator rights rather than as the requesting user."
msgstr "Kunder presenterar en Gitea Personlig tillgång token som ``Authorization: Bearer <token>``. Token utfärdas mot administratörskontot och hålls i ``sys-token-store``. Dess ``auth_subject`` är att ``administrator``, MCP-samtal körs med administratörsrättigheter snarare än som den begärande användaren."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Clients present a long-lived access token as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. The token is minted once per deployment and kept in `sys-token-store` under the `administrator` user, not in the role's `credentials:` block. An unauthenticated request is answered with 404: Home Assistant does not reveal the endpoint."
msgstr "Kunder presenterar en långvarig åtkomsttoken som `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Token präglas en gång per utplacering och hålls i `sys-token-store` under `administrator` användaren, inte i rollens `credentials:` block. En oautentiserad begäran besvaras med 404: Home Assistant avslöjar inte slutpunkten."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Clients present a long-lived access token as ``Authorization: Bearer <token>``. The token is minted once per deployment and kept in ``sys-token-store`` under the ``administrator`` user, not in the role’s ``credentials:`` block. An unauthenticated request is answered with 404: Home Assistant does not reveal the endpoint."
msgstr "Kunder presenterar en långvarig åtkomsttoken som ``Authorization: Bearer <token>``. Token präglas en gång per utplacering och hålls i ``sys-token-store`` under ``administrator`` användaren, inte i rollens ``credentials:`` block. En oautentiserad begäran besvaras med 404: Home Assistant avslöjar inte slutpunkten."

