# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Dual-block resolution: **web-app-bookwyrm** pinned to **flavor: oauth2**; **web-app-gitea** and **web-app-friendica** keep **flavor: oauth2** with the existing *oauth2.acl.blacklist* (*/user/login*) and *oauth2.acl.whitelist* (federation + discovery endpoints) — operative oauth2-proxy gating preserved."
msgstr "Dual-block resolution: **web-app-bookwyrm** Pinned till **smak: oauth2**; **web-app-gitea** och **web-app-friendica** Håll **smak: oauth2** med den befintliga *oauth2.acl.blacklist* (*/user/login*) och *oauth2.acl.whitelist* (Federation + discovery endpoints) operativ oauth2Proxy gating bevarad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Dual-stack model: the node keeps its clearnet ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY``; the node onion is an ADDITIVE address opted-in apps (``services.tor.enabled``) are also reachable under as ``<sub>.<node-onion>`` over Tor. Idempotent: an existing key at ``<base_dir>/.onion-identity/hs`` is reused so the address is stable across runs. The key files are the single source of truth — the ``svc-net-tor`` role copies them into the daemon so it serves exactly this address, and the inventory provisioner writes the returned address into ``applications.svc-net-tor.services.tor.node`` (no env indirection)."
msgstr "Dual-stack modell: noden håller sitt clearnet ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY``; nodlök är en ADDITIVE-adress valda appar (``services.tor.enabled``) är också nåbara under som ``<sub>.<node-onion>`` Tor Idempotent: en befintlig nyckel ``<base_dir>/.onion-identity/hs`` återanvänds så att adressen är stabil över körningar. De viktigaste filerna är den enda källan till sanningen - den ``svc-net-tor`` roll kopierar dem till daemon så det tjänar exakt denna adress, och lagerbäraren skriver den returnerade adressen till ``applications.svc-net-tor.services.tor.node`` (Ingen Env Indirection)."

