msgid "Taiga is ideal for developers, designers, and agile teams who want:"
msgstr "Taiga är idealisk för utvecklare, designers och agila team som vill:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects `/` to the public `/discover` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only `/login` binds the SSO directive (see the note in [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js)). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga's SSO button. Taiga's AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through `ng-click` / `tg-nav` / `ui-sref` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local `test-login-oidc.js` and `test-login-native.js` specs, which enter at `/login` and log out through Taiga's own control."
msgstr "Taiga omdirigeringar `/` till allmänheten `/discover` showcase, som gör en knapp inloggningslänk men inte OIDC ingångspunkt; endast `/login` binder SSO direktivet (se noten i [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js))De delade personerna går alltid in på platsroten, så de kan aldrig nå TaigaSSO knapp. Taiga's AngularJS shell avslöjar dessutom logout endast genom `ng-click` /// `tg-nav` /// `ui-sref` Direktiv, som den generiska inloggningshjälparen inte kan aktivera. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) Därför förklarar `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` och `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; motsvarande resor drivs av roll-lokala `test-login-oidc.js` och `test-login-native.js` specs, som går in på `/login` och logga ut genom Taigaegen kontroll."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects ``/`` to the public ``/discover`` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only ``/login`` binds the SSO directive (see the note in ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` and log out through Taiga’s own control."
msgstr "Taiga omdirigeringar ``/`` till allmänheten ``/discover`` showcase, som gör en knapp inloggningslänk men inte OIDC ingångspunkt; endast ``/login`` binder SSO direktivet (se noten i ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` och logga ut genom Taigaegen kontroll."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Tailored for Arch Linux, this role handles the installation of Firefox using the system’s package manager (``pacman``). It deploys a ``policies.json`` file to Firefox’s distribution directory, ensuring that critical extensions are automatically installed via Firefox Enterprise Policies."
msgstr "Skräddarsydd för Arch Linux, hanterar denna roll installationen av Firefox använda systemets pakethanterare (``pacman``). Det distribuerar en ``policies.json`` fil till Firefoxdistributionskatalog, se till att kritiska tillägg automatiskt installeras via Firefox Enterprise Policies."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Tailored for Arch Linux, this role handles the installation of Firefox using the system’s package manager (`pacman`). It deploys a `policies.json` file to Firefox’s distribution directory, ensuring that critical extensions are automatically installed via Firefox Enterprise Policies."
