# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When NO primary app ships a `meta/variants.yml`, the planner falls back to this path — the `CombinedResolver` walks `dependencies` and `shared:`-edges in the variant-merged services map and Jinja flags are evaluated at deploy time against `group_names`. `run_after` is NOT followed for inclusion (it is a pure ordering hint), so a variant that disables a service does not get the provider re-added through the ordering edge. This module owns the include resolution that path needs and nothing else; the round's variant-merged services maps come from `utils.roles.applications.variants`, which the CI selection resolves its closure from as well."
msgstr "När ingen primär app skickar en `meta/variants.yml`, Planeraren faller tillbaka till denna väg - `CombinedResolver` promenader `dependencies` och `shared:`-edges in the variant-merged services map and Jinja flags are assessmentd at deploy time against `group_names`. `run_after` följs inte för inkludering (Det är en ren beställning tips), så en variant som inaktiverar en tjänst får inte leverantören ombyggd genom beställningskanten. Den här modulen äger den inbegripna upplösningen som vägbehov och inget annat; rundans variant-merged servicekartor kommer från `utils.roles.applications.variants`, som CI-valet löser sin stängning också."

