ead tools of [tools.json](../../roles/web-app-baserow/files/mcp/tools.json), pinned by `schema_sha256`, and lists the ten it refuses under `tools.upstream_serves`, so a version bump that enables one shows up as contract drift instead of as a silently widened surface. The endpoint key reaches the sidecar as `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_KEY` and is spliced in by `policy.upstream_url`, which percent-encodes it, so it never enters the rendered contract. `tasks/utils/mcp.yml` rebuilds the sidecar and runs the adapter probe against it with `list_databases`, which is the deterministic tool call, on every deploy. Baserow was the last role declaring `endpoint.key_credential`, and that field is now gone from the schema, the `roles_with_service` projection and the discovery plugin: a URL segment cannot be scoped per consumer or revoked alone, so a provider that authenticates that way belongs behind an adapter rather than in a client's rendered configuration. The remaining clause, the call arriving from each selected client rather than from the probe, is the end-to-end criterion below."
